[90m|[32m|drives the corresponding pin high as |[90m|
[90m|[32m| soon as possible.  By default most  |[90m|
[90m|[32m| pins come-up as tri-stated inputs.  |[90m|
[90m|[32m|   This feature allows customer to   |[90m|
[90m|[32m|specify active drive pins soon after |[90m|
[90m|[32m|    reset instead of waiting till    |[90m|
[90m|[32m|  complete boot.  Note, if a pin is  |[90m|
[90m|[32m|selected in both QUICK_SET_GPIO_0 and|[90m|
[90m|[32m|QUICK_CLR_GPIO_0 fields then pin will|[90m|
[90m|[32m|   be set to high-level with quick   |[90m|
